    "mainEntity": [
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What does The Regulated Child teach?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The Regulated Child teaches parents to understand their child's behavior through nervous system science. The framework is built on six pillars: The Regulated Brain, Behavior is Body Language, The Regulated Parent, The Regulated Home, Emotions from the Inside Out, and Respond Don't React."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "Why doesn't gentle parenting work for my child?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Most parenting approaches start with the behavior instead of the body. When a child's nervous system is dysregulated, strategies that target behavior — whether firm consequences or gentle language — cannot reach the prefrontal cortex. Co-regulation addresses the body first, which is why it works when other approaches have not."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What is co-regulation and why does it matter?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "Co-regulation is the process of a regulated adult helping a child's nervous system return to a regulated state. Children cannot regulate alone — their nervous systems are built to borrow regulation from the adults around them. Co-regulation works before correction because a dysregulated brain cannot access reasoning, problem-solving, or behavioral change."
        }
      },
      {
        "@type": "Question",
        "name": "What free tools does The Regulated Child offer?",
        "acceptedAnswer": {
          "@type": "Answer",
          "text": "The Regulated Child offers five free tools: Body Behind the Behavior (understanding body signals), Behavior Decoder (six-question nervous system assessment), Co-Regulation Guide (state-matched strategies), In-the-Moment Scripts (what to say during meltdowns), and Regulation Profile Quiz (identifying your child's regulation pattern). All are free, require no account, and take under five minutes."
        }
      }
    ]
  }
  </script>
